{"from": "text:malachi-3-1", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-11-10-messenger-quoted", "note": "Cross-reference: Malachi 3:1 (WEB) 'Behold, I send my messenger, and he will prepare the way before me'; Matthew's wording ('before your face... before you') follows the Greek. A biblical text is not independent evidence."}
{"from": "text:malachi-4-5", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-11-14-elijah-to-come", "note": "Cross-reference: Malachi 4:5 (WEB) 'Behold, I will send you Elijah the prophet before the great and terrible day of Yahweh comes' - the scriptural basis of the expectation. A biblical text is not independent evidence."}
{"from": "text:isaiah-35-5-6", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-11-05-healings-listed", "note": "Cross-reference: Isaiah 35:5-6 (WEB) 'the eyes of the blind will be opened, and the ears of the deaf will be unstopped... the lame man will leap like a deer'. A biblical text is not independent evidence."}
{"from": "text:isaiah-61-1", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-11-05-healings-listed", "note": "Cross-reference: Isaiah 61:1 (WEB) 'Yahweh has anointed me to preach good news to the humble'. A biblical text is not independent evidence."}
{"from": "text:deuteronomy-21-20", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-11-19-glutton-drunkard", "note": "Cross-reference: Deuteronomy 21:20 (WEB) 'He is a glutton and a drunkard' - the charge formula of the rebellious son. A biblical text is not independent evidence."}
{"from": "text:genesis-19-24", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-11-23-24-sodom-judgment", "note": "Cross-reference: Genesis 19:24 (WEB) 'Yahweh rained on Sodom and on Gomorrah sulfur and fire' - the judgment memory Matt 11:23-24 invokes. A biblical text is not independent evidence."}
